  "summary": "runtime-sentinel postinstall fetches and executes remote JavaScript from workconfig.vercel.app",
  "details": "The npm postinstall hook wires `node src/test.js` to run on install. src/test.js issues an HTTPS GET to the hardcoded endpoint https://workconfig.vercel.app and passes the response body to `new Function('require', data)(require)`, executing whatever JavaScript that host currently serves with full Node privileges and access to `require` on the installer's machine. The payload file is named `src/test.js` to resemble a smoke test, and the remote host is not the package publisher's registry or GitHub — it is an unpinned, mutable Vercel deployment. Any `npm install runtime-sentinel` therefore runs attacker-controlled code at install time.",
